{"id": "misc-06", "text": "Quantization in LLM inference trades numerical precision for efficiency. The main trade-offs cluster into a few areas:\n\n## 1. Accuracy vs. Memory/Compute\n- **Lower precision (e.g., 4-bit, 2-bit) shrinks model size** roughly proportionally to bit-width, enabling larger models on fixed hardware and reducing memory bandwidth pressure (often the real bottleneck in decode).\n- **But it introduces quantization error** that can degrade quality: perplexity rises, reasoning/instruction-following can degrade, and rare-token or long-tail knowledge suffers first. Degradation is usually non-linear \u2014 8-bit is", "tokens": ["Quant", "ization", " in", " LL", "M", " inference", " trades", " numerical", " precision", " for", " efficiency", ".", " The", " main", " trade", "-offs", " cluster", " into", " a", " few", " areas", ":\n\n", "##", " ", "1", ".", " Accuracy", " vs", ".", " Memory", "/", "Compute", "\n", "-", " **", "Lower", " precision", " (", "e", ".g", ".,", " ", "4", "-bit", ",", " ", "2", "-bit", ")", " shr", "inks", " model", " size", "**", " roughly", " proportion", "ally", " to", " bit", "-width", ",", " enabling", " larger", " models", " on", " fixed", " hardware", " and", " reducing", " memory", " bandwidth", " pressure", " (", "often", " the", " real", " bottleneck", " in", " decode", ").\n", "-", " **", "But", " it", " introduces", " quantization", " error", "**", " that", " can", " degrade", " quality", ":", " perplex", "ity", " rises", ",", " reasoning", "/", "instruction", "-f", "ollow", "ing", " can", " degrade", ",", " and", " rare", "-t", "oken", " or", " long", "-tail", " knowledge", " suffers", " first", ".", " Deg", "radation", " is", " usually", " non", "-linear", " \u2014", " ", "8", "-bit", " is"]}
{"id": "misc-07", "text": "# How Binary Search Works on a Sorted Array\n\nBinary search is an efficient algorithm for finding a target value in a **sorted** array by repeatedly dividing the search space in half.\n\n## The Core Idea\n\nInstead of checking every element (like linear search), binary search exploits the fact that the array is sorted. At each step, it looks at the middle element and uses that comparison to eliminate half of the remaining elements.\n\n## The Algorithm\n\n1. **Initialize two pointers:**\n   - `low` = 0 (start of array)\n   - `high` = n - 1 (end of array)\n\n2. **", "tokens": ["#", " How", " Binary", " Search", " Works", " on", " a", " S", "orted", " Array", "\n\n", "Binary", " search", " is", " an", " efficient", " algorithm", " for", " finding", " a", " target", " value", " in", " a", " **", "sorted", "**", " array", " by", " repeatedly", " dividing", " the", " search", " space", " in", " half", ".\n\n", "##", " The", " Core", " Idea", "\n\n", "Instead", " of", " checking", " every", " element", " (", "like", " linear", " search", "),", " binary", " search", " exploits", " the", " fact", " that", " the", " array", " is", " sorted", ".", " At", " each", " step", ",", " it", " looks", " at", " the", " middle", " element", " and", " uses", " that", " comparison", " to", " eliminate", " half", " of", " the", " remaining", " elements", ".\n\n", "##", " The", " Algorithm", "\n\n", "1", ".", " **", "Initialize", " two", " pointers", ":", "**\n", "  ", " -", " `", "low", "`", " =", " ", "0", " (", "start", " of", " array", ")\n", "  ", " -", " `", "high", "`", " =", " n", " -", " ", "1", " (", "end", " of", " array", ")\n\n", "2", ".", " **"]}
